---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AppHeader from '../components/AppHeader.astro';

export const prerender = false;
---

<Layout title="What this scan can and cannot test · Us" indexable={true} authMode="guest-ok">
  <div class="app-shell">
    <AppHeader crumb="Limitations" />
    <main class="app-main">
      <article class="container-narrow" style="padding: clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px) 0 clamp(48px, 8vw, 96px);">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Honesty · WCAG 2.2 AA · EN 301 549</span>
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(32px, 4.5vw, 48px); margin: 12px 0 16px;">What this tool can and cannot claim</h1>
        <p class="p-large muted" style="max-width: 640px;">
          This product is an <strong>assisted automated scanner</strong>. It finds many issues that machines can find.
          It is <strong>not</strong> a complete WCAG 2.2 AA audit, not EN 301 549 certification, and not an EAA legal sign-off.
        </p>

        <section style="margin-top: 40px;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 22px; margin-bottom: 10px;">What we run</h2>
          <ul class="muted" style="padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; max-width: 640px;">
            <li>axe-core rules tagged WCAG 2.0 / 2.1 / 2.2 Level A and AA (not best-practice-as-AA).</li>
            <li>Custom checks for structure, images, contrast, 320px reflow, forms, names, and a few dynamic-content heuristics.</li>
            <li>Axe “incomplete” items as <em>needs review</em>, not as passes.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 32px;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 22px; margin-bottom: 10px;">What we cannot test automatically</h2>
          <ul class="muted" style="padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; max-width: 640px;">
            <li>Real screen-reader, keyboard, and cognitive testing with people.</li>
            <li>Most of WCAG 2.2’s 50 Level A and AA success criteria (captions quality, meaningful sequence, language of parts, accessible authentication, and more).</li>
            <li>Client-rendered SPAs if content is not in the DOM at scan time.</li>
            <li>YouTube / Vimeo and other embedded players (captions must be checked by a human).</li>
            <li>Pages behind login, CAPTCHA, or bot protection.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 32px;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 22px; margin-bottom: 10px;">How to read the score</h2>
          <p class="muted" style="max-width: 640px;">
            The 0–100 figure is the share of <em>applicable automated checks that passed</em> on this run.
            Easy environment checks (for example “no meta refresh”) are excluded so they do not inflate the number.
            A high score does not mean the site conforms. A low score does not mean it fails every criterion.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section style="margin-top: 32px;">
          <h2 style="font-size: 22px; margin-bottom: 10px;">European Accessibility Act</h2>
          <p class="muted" style="max-width: 640px;">
            Since 28 June 2025 the EAA applies to listed consumer services in the EU (for example e-commerce),
            with a micro-enterprise exemption. It does <strong>not</strong> automatically apply to every website.
            EN 301 549 is the usual technical reference. This tool helps you find issues; it does not certify EAA compliance.
          </p>
        </section>

        <p style="margin-top: 40px;">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/">Run a free 1-page scan</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>
